/-
  HVFalse/Proofs/Bracket.lean - Prop. 10 (bracket), the `s₊` side (claim C19a): (HV) fails on `[s₊(p), sec²(π/2p)]` at the
  six `p` of the table
  Copyright (C) Dave Goel 2026--now. All rights reserved.

  Route: Prop. fail (`prop_fail`, TheoremA.lean) needs ONE point with `Γ(y,t) < e(t)` at `s₊`; `Γ` decreases in `s`
  (`gam_antitone_s`), so the point serves every `s ∈ [s₊, sec²ϑ]`. The points are the certificate's Arb points
  (logs/bracket_upper_arb.log) rounded to 4 decimals. Each `Γ < e` is reduced (`gam_lt_ee_of_bounds`) to rational
  checks: `cos ϑ` from Taylor at rational `ϑ±` (Mathlib's 20-digit π bounds, `cos` monotone), `cosh` from `exp` Taylor,
  `x^(m/n)` by integer powers, and the exponent `p/s` replaced by a smaller rational `a/b` (`cosh ≥ 1`). No interval
  arithmetic, no native code. The certificates were generated and re-checked exactly (Python `Fraction`) by gen.py/emit.py,
  generated by a script (not shipped).
-/
